# On the natural gradient for variational quantum eigensolver

Naoki Yamamoto — Keio University — 11 Sep 2019 — arXiv:1909.05074

## Abstract (paraphrased from paper)

The natural-gradient method, originally developed in information geometry for classical
statistical learning, has recently been extended to variational quantum optimization by
Stokes et al. (arXiv:1909.02108), where the Fisher-information metric is replaced by the
Fubini–Study (quantum information) metric. This note analyzes three worked examples --- a
single-qubit driving Hamiltonian, a reduced two-qubit H₂ Hamiltonian, and a near-separable
toy molecule --- to illustrate when the quantum natural gradient (QNG) accelerates convergence
of VQE, and when it fails.

